<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4022.18">
  <DUT Name="ST_Proportionair" Id="{1cb50253-0c45-4afc-8e14-284b1dbf64b6}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    Purpose: interface structure for one Proportionair electronic pressure
    regulator channel. It carries the pressure setpoint and its limits, the
    regulated-pressure readback, the controller stability flag, and the two raw
    analog terminal words that bind the structure to the field wiring.

    Usage: instantiated once per regulator inside a pressure control module
    (stPropAir1/stPropAir2 of FB_PressureControlModule and of FB_MPV1) and
    passed to the owning regulator FB through its VAR_IN_OUT iq_stRegProp:
        FB_PCM_AIO                (FB_MPV1, full scale 100 psi)
        FB_ProportionairRegulator (FB_PressureControlModule, full scale 1000)
    The owning FB, not this structure, holds the scale: each scan it derives
    iPressure from i_iPressRB, clamps iSetpoint into [iLoLimit, iHiLimit] and
    derives q_iPressCt from the clamped setpoint. i_iPressRB and q_iPressCt are
    the only members that reach the field; the deployment program links them to
    the EtherCAT analog terminal with a TcLinkTo pragma (see
    EXAMPLE_DEPLOYMENT, which binds them to the EP4374-0002 AI/AO channels of
    "PCM A").

    Objectives:
    - One named interface per regulator, so that the deployment program, the
      regulator FB and the EPICS records use the same variable names.
    - Keep the engineering values (setpoint, limits, pressure) in the
      regulator's own unit and the terminal words in raw counts, so that the
      two are never confused.
    - Publish the same members to EPICS through the pytmc pragmas below
      (Enable, Setpoint, HighLimit, LowLimit, Pressure).

    Units, and the caveat on them: the pressure members are integers in psi
    against a 0-10 V terminal span, 0..100 psi mapped onto 0..32767 counts.
    That is the scale FB_PCM_AIO states (iDEVICE_MAX_PRESSURE := 100 // (psi),
    iTermBits := 32767) and the scale FB_MPV1 passes to it.
    FB_ProportionairRegulator instead maps the span onto 0..1000 and comments
    it as "max pressure out 1000 (I think...)", so on a module driven by that
    FB the pressure members run 0..1000 and are not psi. Nothing in this
    repository records the pressure span of the installed regulators: treat psi
    as FB_PCM_AIO's claim, not as a measurement of the hardware.

    History:
    2023-05-19 J. Zamudio - structure added with the initial commit (746deac);
    xStable was the only member carrying a comment.
    2025-05-29 J. Zamudio - moved to Library/DUTs in the project restructure
    (9b2fb2c), contents unchanged.
    2026-11-27 header and per-member comments added; no member, type or pragma
    changed (convention audit, task #125).
*)
TYPE ST_Proportionair :
STRUCT

(* Control, written from EPICS *)
{attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: Enable
        io: io
     '}
xEnable	:	BOOL;	// Regulation enable request. Published as PropAir:0n:Enable but read by no regulator FB - see header.
{attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: Setpoint
        io: io
     '}
iSetpoint	:	INT;	// Pressure setpoint, psi (0..100 on a 100 psi span). Clamped into [iLoLimit, iHiLimit] by the owning FB.
{attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: HighLimit
        io: io
     '}
iHiLimit	:	INT;	// Upper clamp for iSetpoint, psi (0..100). No default in the FBs: 0 until set from EPICS.
{attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: LowLimit
        io: io
     '}
iLoLimit	:	INT;	// Lower clamp for iSetpoint, psi (0..100). No default in the FBs: 0 until set from EPICS.

(* Readback *)
xStable	: BOOL;//TTL signal from the proportionair controller that the pressure is stable
{attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: Pressure
        io: i
     '}
iPressure : INT;	// Measured pressure, psi (0..100), scaled by the owning FB from i_iPressRB. Read-only to EPICS.

(* Raw analog terminal words: the only members that reach the field *)
{attribute 'TcDisplayScale' := '0-10'}
i_iPressRB AT %I* : INT;	// Analog input counts, 0..32767 = 0..10 V = 0..100 psi (FB_PCM_AIO span); negatives clamped to 0.
{attribute 'TcDisplayScale' := '0-10'}
q_iPressCt AT %Q* : INT;	// Analog output counts, 0..32767 = 0..10 V = 0..100 psi pressure demand to the regulator.

END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>